# GC573 experiment: audio capture with the M4 driver (spec/audio.md "Unknown", open question 5)
date:    2026-11-25 04:40-05:45 UTC
vm:      gc573-dev, kernel 6.8.0-151-generic
source:  host DVI-D-0 (GT 710, NVIDIA 470) 1920x1080p60; tools/testsrc/avsync.sh (bursts: one 60 Hz frame,
         800 samples, half scale, left 1 kHz, right 2 kHz, once a second) where noted
tools:   tests/gc573-aud.c (-v: per read frames, hw pointer, ALSA timestamp, peaks; -M: AUDIO_SAMPLE_PERIOD,
         AUDIO_DONE, DMA_RUN from BAR0), tests/live-av.py, per-burst alignment check (lr.py, below)
driver:  the M4 driver as committed, at the stage noted per run; exp_audio_raw / exp_audio_fill as noted

## 1. No input (IT6805 audio WAIT_READY, AUDIO_SAMPLE_PERIOD 0xffffffff), exp_audio_raw=1, exp_audio_fill=0x5a5a
3 s: 300 periods, AUDIO_DONE 1, 2, 1, 2, intervals 9.820-10.176 ms, INT bit 4 at the stop.
Every sample 0: the fill written into each buffer after its copy never came back, so the FPGA
writes every period, zeros without input. Rate 48000.255 Hz against CLOCK_MONOTONIC.
  RESULT audio frames=144000 secs=2.990 rate=48000.255 xruns=0 restarts=0
  reads 300, with a nonzero sample 0

